  "meshOriginUU": [
   -150,
   40,
   0
  ],
  "orientationNote": "Vertices are mesh-frame, so they reach the actor frame through the TRANSPOSE of UE1's FRotationMatrix(RotOrigin), with Mesh.Origin subtracted before Mesh.Scale. UE1 pawns face +X, so through UT (x fwd, y right, z up) -> world (x right, y up, z back) every body faces -Z with no per-model yaw. See scripts/build-ut-characters.mjs.",
